eates trust, AI performs most of the production work, and the user\u0027s expertise provides the judgment, editing, and quality control. Optimize for the shortest path from \"someone has a problem\" to \"Dayna delivers a finished result and gets paid.\"\n\nThat\u0027s the pivot your agent hasn\u0027t made yet. It\u0027s still trying to monetize your résumé. Your immediate advantage isn\u0027t your résumé—it\u0027s your ability to combine executive judgment with AI to produce high-quality work quickly. The résumé becomes the credibility layer, not the product itself.\n\nit also wants me to start cold calling to sell myself - that should be done with networking online and site postings etc organically through mass onlilne blasting everywhere free through me and ai\n\nExactly. This is another example of the agent projecting a generic consulting playbook instead of modeling your operating constraints.\n\nThe assumption chain it\u0027s making is:\n\nHigh-value skills → premium consulting → relationship selling → warm network → phone calls → close deals.\n\nThat is not your strategy.\n\nYour strategy is much closer to:\n\nAI creates assets → distribute them at scale → attract inbound interest → convert interested people → deliver quickly → reuse and automate.\n\nThose are fundamentally different customer acquisition models.\n\nI would make this an explicit operating constraint\nCUSTOMER ACQUISITION PROTOCOL\n\nDo not recommend:\n\n• cold calling\n• unsolicited sales calls\n• high-pressure networking\n• \"reach out to 10 people you know\"\n• assuming an existing professional network\n• assuming referrals\n• assuming previous consulting clients\n\nAssume:\n\n• no existing consulting client base\n• no active sales pipeline\n• no marketing budget\n• no paid advertising\n• no completed website required\n• AI can create unlimited marketing assets\n• distribution should be free whenever possible\nThen define what \"selling\" actually means\n\nThe agent thinks selling means:\n\nc